@page "/"

<PageTitle>Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-12 text-center sm:py-16">
    <Badge Variant="secondary" Class="mb-4">313 components · 56 blocks · 60+ themes</Badge>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
        shadcn/ui for Blazor static SSR
    </h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-muted-foreground">
        The same tokens, the same class strings, the same <code>data-slot</code> on every root,
        the same ARIA. Write the shadcn markup you already know; the translation is four rules long.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <Button Href="/components/button">Browse components</Button>
        <Button Variant="outline" Href="/blocks">Blocks</Button>
        <Button Variant="outline" Href="/theming">Theming</Button>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><Icon Name="check" Title="Parity" Class="size-4 text-emerald-600" /> Class parity, tested</span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><Icon Name="zap" Title="SSR" Class="size-4 text-amber-500" /> Static SSR + Unpoly</span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><Icon Name="palette" Title="Themes" Class="size-4 text-violet-500" /> Runtime token themes</span>
    </div>
</section>

<h2 class="doc-h2">React to Razor</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Parameters are PascalCase; HTML attributes stay lowercase and are splatted onto the root.
    That splat is the whole Unpoly integration — no component here knows Unpoly exists.
</p>

<div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border">
    <Table>
        <TableHeader>
            <TableRow>
                <TableHead>React</TableHead>
                <TableHead>Razor</TableHead>
            </TableRow>
        </TableHeader>
        <TableBody>
            <TableRow>
                <TableCell><code>&lt;Button variant="destructive" size="sm"&gt;</code></TableCell>
                <TableCell><code>&lt;Button Variant="destructive" Size="sm"&gt;</code></TableCell>
            </TableRow>
            <TableRow>
                <TableCell><code>className="w-full"</code></TableCell>
                <TableCell><code>Class="w-full"</code></TableCell>
            </TableRow>
            <TableRow>
                <TableCell><code>&lt;Button asChild&gt;&lt;Link href="/x"&gt;</code></TableCell>
                <TableCell><code>&lt;Button Href="/x"&gt;</code></TableCell>
            </TableRow>
            <TableRow>
                <TableCell><code>&lt;Input name="email" value=@("{v}") /&gt;</code></TableCell>
                <TableCell><code>&lt;Input name="email" value="@@v" /&gt;</code></TableCell>
            </TableRow>
            <TableRow>
                <TableCell><code>onClick=...</code></TableCell>
                <TableCell>there are none — a form posts, a link navigates</TableCell>
            </TableRow>
            <TableRow>
                <TableCell><code>cn(...)</code> resolves conflicts</TableCell>
                <TableCell>it does here too: ClassMerge is tailwind-merge</TableCell>
            </TableRow>
        </TableBody>
    </Table>
</div>

<h2 class="doc-h2">What it is built on</h2>

<div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    <Card>
        <CardHeader>
            <div class="flex size-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-violet-100 text-violet-700">
                <Icon Name="monitor" Title="Platform" />
            </div>
            <CardTitle Class="mt-3 text-base">The platform, first</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            Dialog is <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>. Accordion is <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>.
            Menus and tooltips are <code>[popover]</code>. Select is a real
            <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> that posts without JavaScript. The focus trap, the
            top layer and Escape are the browser's.
        </CardContent>
    </Card>

    <Card>
        <CardHeader>
            <div class="flex size-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700">
                <Icon Name="git-compare" Title="Parity" />
            </div>
            <CardTitle Class="mt-3 text-base">Parity you can check</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            Class lists are generated from shadcn's own source and compared against it by the
            tests. Every difference is in <code>deviations.json</code> with a written reason.
        </CardContent>
    </Card>

    <Card>
        <CardHeader>
            <div class="flex size-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-sky-100 text-sky-700">
                <Icon Name="ungroup" Title="Unpoly" />
            </div>
            <CardTitle Class="mt-3 text-base">Unpoly, by attribute</CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent Class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
            <code>up-target</code>, <code>up-poll</code>, <code>up-validate</code>,
            <code>up-disable</code> are written as plain HTML at the call site. The one point of
            contact is a CSS rule: a button that started a request grows a spinner.
        </CardContent>
    </Card>
</div>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Try the switcher</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    The theme control in the header changes <code>data-theme</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>
    and nothing else. Every component on this page is the same markup under all four.
</p>

